---
// Utilities: rate cases on the record — requested vs granted (qualitative survey Build 12;
// docs/qualitative-desks-survey.md §Utilities P2). QUOTE-ONLY: every figure the reader sees is
// a verbatim substring of the filed sentence beside it, and the lane never computes, totals or
// restates a number. ALWAYS A LIST — a utility of any size is several proceedings at once, and
// a single row would be a chosen one. NO STATUS FIELD: the survey refused pending/decided/
// expected on measured staleness, so a row says what the filer said and when, and nothing about
// what happens next.
//
// Placement: the utility PRICING slot, immediately after the scorecard, where a non-financial
// company's pricing read renders (moatReport → pricingReconciliation) and a rate-regulated one
// has none — the utilities desk measured zero of sixty issuers firing on pricing power, because
// tariffed rates mean competitive-pricing language does not exist in these filings. What sets a
// utility's price is a commission, case by case, and this is that record. Build 10's
// disallowance ledger continues further down the act, beside the debt ladder.
//
// The substring identity is asserted at extraction time and RE-CHECKED here (the Build 9/10
// precedent), so a record that drifts from its quote retires rather than render. Utilities only,
// on the rateRegulated flag — the desk's own tag census, never SIC.
import language from "../data/language.json";

const { company } = Astro.props;
const rec = company?.rateRegulated ? (language?.companies?.[company?.ticker] || null) : null;
const rc = rec?.rateCases || null;

// Render-time weld re-check: a figure that is not the quote's own characters, or a case name
// that is neither the quote's nor its heading's, retires the row.
const ok = (r) =>
  r?.quote &&
  (r.figures || []).length > 0 &&
  (r.figures || []).every((f) => f?.text && r.quote.includes(f.text)) &&
  r.label &&
  (r.quote.includes(r.label) || (r.heading && r.heading.includes(r.label)));
const cases = (rc?.cases || []).filter(ok);
const withheld = !cases.length && rc?.withheld?.quote ? rc.withheld : null;
const show = cases.length || withheld;

const roleLabel = { requirement: "revenue requirement", roe: "return on equity", rateBase: "rate base", pct: "percent" };
const kindLabel = (k) => (k === "granted" ? "granted by the commission" : "requested by the filer");
---

{show ? (
  <section class="rcase">
    <div class="head">
      <h3 class="secTitle">Rate cases, in the filing&rsquo;s words</h3>
      <div class="hmeta">
        {rc.fy ? <span class="asof">FY{rc.fy} 10-K</span> : null}
        {rec?.sourceUrl ? <a class="src" href={rec.sourceUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">the filing, SEC EDGAR &rarr;</a> : null}
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="intro">
      A regulated utility does not set its own price. It asks a commission for one, case by case, and the commission
      grants some part of it. Below are the proceedings this filing puts on the record, quoted verbatim, largest
      dollars first. Nothing here is computed; every figure is the filer&rsquo;s own sentence.
    </p>

    {cases.length ? (
      <ul class="rows">
        {cases.map((r) => (
          <li class="row">
            <div class="rhead">
              <span class="case">{r.label}</span>
              <span class={`tag ${r.kind}`}>{kindLabel(r.kind)}</span>
            </div>
            <div class="chips">
              {r.figures.map((f) => (
                <span class="chip">
                  {roleLabel[f.role] ? <span class="role">{roleLabel[f.role]}</span> : null}
                  <span class="fig">{f.text}</span>
                </span>
              ))}
            </div>
            <blockquote class="q">&ldquo;{r.quote}&rdquo;</blockquote>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    ) : null}

    {withheld ? (
      <div class="withheld">
        <p class="lab">No rate case on this record, and the filer says why</p>
        <blockquote class="q">&ldquo;{withheld.quote}&rdquo;</blockquote>
      </div>
    ) : null}

    <p class="foot">
      Sentences from the Regulatory Matters and Pending Proceedings disclosures and the MD&amp;A of the latest 10-K,
      largest dollars first, at most six. &ldquo;Granted&rdquo; marks a sentence in which the commission itself is the
      subject of the approving verb; everything else renders as a request, never as a decided outcome. A return on
      equity is shown only where the filer states one between 8 and 13 percent &mdash; the same figure in these
      filings also carries equity ratios and fair-value returns, and a number that must be interpreted before it can
      be believed is not shown at all. Nothing here says whether a case is still pending: filings state timings that
      are already past by the time they are read.
    </p>
  </section>
) : null}

<style>
  .rcase { margin: 24px 0; }
  .head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); padding-bottom: 6px; }
  .secTitle { margin: 0; }
  .hmeta { display: inline-flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: flex-end; }
  .asof { font-size: 11.5px; letter-spacing: 0.03em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); flex: 0 0 auto; }
  .src { font-size: 12px; color: var(--accent); flex: 0 0 auto; }
  .intro { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted); margin: 9px 0 0; max-width: 74ch; line-height: 1.6; }

  .rows { list-style: none; margin: 16px 0 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 16px; }
  .row { border-left: 2px solid var(--rule-strong); padding: 2px 0 2px 12px; }
  .rhead { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .case { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); }
  .tag { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: 0.04em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .tag.granted { color: var(--accent); }

  .chips { display: flex; align-items: stretch; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 6px 0 0; }
  .chip { display: inline-flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1px; border: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); padding: 2px 7px; }
  .role { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 9.5px; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); }
  .fig { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 12.5px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }

  .q { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--ink-soft); margin: 7px 0 0; max-width: 78ch; }

  .withheld { margin: 16px 0 0; border-left: 2px solid var(--rule-strong); padding: 2px 0 2px 12px; }
  .lab { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 0.05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }

  .foot { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted); border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-strong); margin-top: 16px; padding-top: 10px; max-width: 78ch; }
</style>
